  (text "DESIGN NOTES (ARCHITECTURE & SIGNAL-INTEGRITY REVIEW FIXES):\n1. 250mA PPTC FUSE F1, SERIES P-MOSFET REVERSE-POLARITY SWITCH Q2, TRANSIENT ESD REFERENCE D1 & 18V-VIN LDO (arch.review/001, 002):\n   - J1 VBUS feeds USB_VBUS -> F1 (BSMD0603-025-24V, C7543776, I_hold = 250 mA @ 25 C / 190 mA >= 150 mA @ 50 C, I_trip = 550 mA, 24 V, R_min = 0.50 Ohm, R_1max = 3.0 Ohm) -> VBUS_FUSED -> Q2 (AO3401A, C15127, 30V 4A P-MOSFET reverse-polarity switch, R_DS(on) <= 60 mOhm @ V_GS = -4.5 V; Gate VBUS_Q2_G pulled to GND via 10k R15 and clamped to Source by 8.2V Zener D6 BZT52C8V2S C22375294 so |V_GS| <= 8.7 V < 12 V abs max) -> VBUS_PROT.\n   - During reverse polarity on USB_VBUS (down to -24 V), Q2 is completely OFF (V_GS = 0 V, body diode reverse-biased), isolating VBUS_PROT, D1, and 5V_USB_MOUSE / U3 (ME6209A33M3G, VIN_min = -0.3 V) at 0.00 V. D1 (USBLC6-2SC6, C2687116) pin 5 and C11 (1 uF 50V) sit on VBUS_PROT solely as the 8/20 us IEC 61000-4-2 transient ESD clamp reference (never as a DC crowbar).\n   - VBUS_PROT -> FB1 (BLM18PG121SN1D, 50 mOhm) -> VBUS_FB -> R11 (HP06W2F120KT5E, C414958, 1.2 Ohm 1% 500 mW 1206) -> 5V_USB_MOUSE (C1 1 uF 50V) provides critical LC hot-plug damping (R_total,min = 1.79 Ohm, zeta_min = 0.895 > 0.707; R_total,typ = 2.39 Ohm, zeta_typ = 1.195 > 1.0) while keeping worst-case post-reflow series drop at 0.220 V (@ 51.1 mA), 0.345 V (@ 80 mA), 0.431 V < 0.50 V (@ 100 mA), and F1 drop 0.450 V < 0.50 V (@ 150 mA, V_IN(U3) = 4.103 V >= 3.666 V with +0.437 V LDO dropout headroom). At F1 I_trip = 550 mA, R11 dissipates 0.363 W <= 0.50 W.\n2. ST AN4080 4.7uF VDD BULK RESERVOIR C2 & LOCAL 1uF VDDA BULK BYPASS C15 (arch.review/003):\n   - 3V3_MOUSE is decoupled at U3/U4 by C2 (CL10A475KA8NQNC, C69335, 4.7 uF 25V X5R) and locally at U1.5 (VDDA) / U1.1 (VDD) by C15 (CC0603KRX7R9BB105, C559769, 1 uF 50V X7R) in parallel with C7 (100 nF) + C13 (10 nF) per ST AN4080 Section 3.1.1/3.1.2 (direct 5V C_RPB = C11 + C1 = 2.0 uF in [1, 10] uF; total rail-weighted charge Q = 48.22 uC <= 50 uC).\n3. BOOT0 HARDWARE RC DEBOUNCE C14 & SENSOR RESET SEQUENCING (arch.review/004):\n   - C14 (CC0603KRX7R9BB104, C14663, 100 nF 50V X7R) on MCU_BOOT0 (U1.31 PB8/BOOT0) provides 1.0 ms hold time (R3 10k * 100nF) across SW2 contact bounce gaps and 0.10 ms charge time via R8 (1k), preventing bounce races during NVIC_SystemReset() or cold-boot USB DFU entry."
